#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-author-privacy.php:350
msgid "Author archives are currently disabled site-wide in Settings, Dashboard Cleanup."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-author-privacy.php:355
msgid "Author Archive"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-author-privacy.php:356
msgid "Disable this user's author archive page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:148
msgid "XML-RPC is now disabled. Jetpack and the WordPress mobile apps will not be able to reach this site until you turn it back off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:169
msgid "Author Privacy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:170
msgid "These options reduce what your site publishes about the people who write on it. They change public URLs and API responses, so review your site and your search console after turning any of them on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:174
msgid "Author archives"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:175
msgid "Disable author archive pages site-wide"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:176
msgid "Visitors requesting an author archive get your theme's 404 page. You can also disable a single author's archive from their profile screen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:180
msgid "Author enumeration"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:181
msgid "Block requests that look up an author by ID"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:182
msgid "A request like /?author=1 normally redirects to the author's archive URL, which reveals their username. This returns a 404 instead. It has no effect on sites using plain permalinks, where /?author=1 is the real author archive URL."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:186
msgid "REST API users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:187
msgid "Hide the users endpoint from logged-out visitors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:188
msgid "Removes /wp-json/wp/v2/users for anyone who is not logged in. Logged-in users are unaffected, so the block editor keeps working. Author details will stop appearing in embedded REST responses for anonymous requests."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:192
msgid "Author sitemap"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:193
msgid "Leave authors out of the WordPress sitemap"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:194
msgid "Removes the users section from /wp-sitemap.xml. This also happens automatically when author archives are disabled site-wide."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:198
msgid "oEmbed author data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:199
msgid "Remove author name and URL from oEmbed responses"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:200
msgid "Applies to both the JSON and XML oEmbed output other sites request when they embed your posts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:206
msgid "Fingerprint Reduction"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:207
msgid "These options remove version strings and discovery links that identify your WordPress install to automated scanners. They do not change how your site looks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:211
msgid "Generator tag"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:212
msgid "Remove the WordPress version from pages and feeds"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:213
msgid "Removes the generator meta tag from the page head and the generator element from every feed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:217
msgid "RSD link"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:218
msgid "Remove the Really Simple Discovery link"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:219
msgid "Used only by remote publishing clients over XML-RPC. WordPress 6.7 and later no longer output it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:223
msgid "Windows Live Writer link"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:224
msgid "Remove the Windows Live Writer manifest link"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:225
msgid "Windows Live Writer was retired in 2017. WordPress 6.7 and later no longer output this link."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:229
msgid "Shortlink"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:230
msgid "Remove the shortlink tag and HTTP header"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:231
msgid "Removes both the shortlink element from the page head and the matching Link header from the response."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:235
msgid "XML-RPC"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:236
msgid "Reject all XML-RPC method calls"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:237
msgid "Check what uses this first. Disabling XML-RPC breaks the Jetpack connection, the official WordPress mobile apps, and any plugin or service that posts to your site remotely. If Jetpack is active, leave this off. Blocking xmlrpc.php at your web server is stronger than blocking it here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:241
msgid "Pingbacks"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:242
msgid "Remove the pingback method and X-Pingback header"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:243
msgid "Pingbacks can be used to bounce traffic off your site at someone else. This leaves the rest of XML-RPC working. Disabling XML-RPC above already covers this."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:273
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ph-cleanup-settings.php:383
msgid "Everything on this page is off by default. Turn on only what your site needs."
msgstr ""

